---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { getFragments } from '../lib/fragments';

const fragments = await getFragments();
---

<Base
  title="About — The Silent Campaign"
  description="How fragment-based publication works for The Silent Campaign."
>
  <section class="container page-head">
    <p class="page-eyebrow label">About</p>
    <h1 class="page-title">How to read it</h1>
  </section>

  <section class="container prose">
    <p>
      <em>The Silent Campaign</em> is a novel published in fragments, in the order it is
      written. Each fragment is a self-contained scene: it can be read on its own, while
      the running count preserves the sequence. There are currently {fragments.length} online.
    </p>
    <p>
      The fragments have no titles. A title would anticipate too much, and here that would
      spoil the pace: they are simply counted. The number shows the fragment&rsquo;s position in
      the novel; the date shows when it was published.
    </p>

    <h2>Where to find them</h2>
    <p>
      The <a href="/archive/">archive</a> collects everything published so far. Those who
      prefer to receive fragments as they appear can follow the <a href="/rss.xml">RSS feed</a>:
      every new release arrives with the same name it has on the site.
    </p>

    <h2>The text</h2>
    <p>
      The pages on this site are demonstration text: they show the layout rather than tell
      the final story. The novel changes as it progresses, and already published fragments
      may be revised; their date remains the date of first publication.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      For feedback, corrections, or discussion: <a href="mailto:editorial@thesilentcampaign.com"
        >editorial@thesilentcampaign.com</a
      >.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
